              "kind": "text",
              "key": "q8_1",
              "accepted": [
                "Spur teeth require simple straight-axis hobbing or shaping with standard tooling; they require no helix lead generation, workhead swiveling, or differential gear trains"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "key": "q8_2",
              "accepted": [
                "Spur gears are relatively forgiving of slight axial displacement; Helical gears are highly sensitive to axial position and lead alignment because axial shifts alter tooth contact across the face width"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "key": "q8_3",
              "accepted": [
                "Lower replacement cost, readily available standard radial bearings, and straightforward field assembly without complex bearing preloading (shimming)"
              ]
            },
