              "accepted": [
                "Spur Gear — Low pitch velocity (v = 1.2 m/s) avoids noise issues; zero axial thrust simplifies bearing arrangements; rugged and economical for field maintenance"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "key": "q9_2",
              "accepted": [
                "Helical Gear — High pitch velocity (v = 25 m/s) and strict noise limit (< 65 dBA) mandate progressive tooth engagement and high overlap contact ratio to eliminate gear whine"
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "key": "q9_3",
              "accepted": [
                "Spur Gear — Hand-powered intermittent operation has negligible dynamic excitation; zero axial thrust allows economical radial journal bushings without thrust bearings"
              ]
            },
